OL,3,GNEWSAInconceivable security forces were
OL,4,Anot involved in killing, court hears
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt is "inconceivable" that the loyalist
OL,7,Fkilling of a Gaelic football fan during
OL,8,Fthe Troubles could have been planned
OL,9,Fand carried out without the involvement
OL,10,Fof the security forces, a court has
OL,11,Fbeen told.
OL,13,FSean Farmer, 32, was on his way home
OL,14,Ffrom a GAA match when he was shot dead
OL,15,Falong with his friend Colm McCartney,
OL,16,F22, at a dummy roadblock in
OL,17,FAltnamackin, County Armagh, in 1975.
OL,19,FFarmer's family has taken a civil case
OL,20,Fagainst the Ministry of Defence (MoD)
OL,21,Falleging misfeasance in public office,
OL,22,Fnegligence and trespass to the person.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
